course: dictionary
lesson: 12544
title: A word that decides
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: A determinant is something that decides what happens, or strongly affects it. Think of it as a cause that shapes the result. Clue: if a sentence is about what makes something happen or not, a determinant is probably involved.
explain: «Sleep is a big determinant of how well you learn.» Sleep does not just happen alongside learning. It strongly affects how well you learn, so sleep is a determinant.
explain: «Climate is a determinant of where people live.» The weather pattern of a place helps to decide where people choose to live. The word is formal, so you will meet it mostly in science, health and geography writing.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. In «Sleep is a big factor in how well you learn», the sentence still makes sense, so factor is a useful stand-in. The maths meaning is different, and you will learn it later.
fact: A determinant is a noun: one determinant, two or more determinants.
fact: «Determinant» means something that decides or strongly affects what happens.
fact: «Diet and exercise are determinants of health.» Here determinants means factors that shape how healthy you are.
fact: In maths, a determinant is a special number worked out from a square table of numbers, called a matrix. This is used in higher maths and is not usually taught at primary school.
fact: The word is rare in everyday talk, so it is a good one to recognise in reading and to use carefully in writing.
exercise: «Sleep is a big determinant of how well you learn.» What is a determinant in this sentence? | *Something that strongly affects what happens | A type of soft bed | A shape with four equal sides | A loud noise in class
exercise: «Diet and exercise are determinants of health.» Which word could replace determinants without changing the meaning? | *Factors | Pictures | Mistakes | Holidays
exercise: In maths, a determinant is worked out from a square table of numbers. What is that table called? | A sentence | A bar chart | A decimal | *A matrix
test: «Rain is a determinant of how green the fields are.» What does determinant mean here? | A small field | A green paint colour | A grey cloud | *Something that decides or strongly affects it
test: Which of these is a determinant of how fast a plant grows? | Its favourite song | The day of the week | *Sunlight and water | The name of the gardener
exam: Which sentence uses determinant correctly? | "The determinant was bright blue." | "I ate a determinant for lunch." | "The determinant ran across the playground." | *"Money is a determinant of whether a family can buy a house."
